<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tabula Rogeriana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1154</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Book of Roger, Kitab Rujar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tabula Rogeriana, or Book of Roger, is the great work of geography that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-idrisi">Muhammad al-Idrisi</a> completed in 1154 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a>. Written in Arabic and drawing on earlier geographers and travellers' reports gathered at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> court, it describes the known world from the Atlantic to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> with a world map divided into seventy sectional maps. It remained one of the most accurate world maps for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tabula-rogeriana.jpg" alt="Tabula Rogeriana" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown copyist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:89v_90r_%D9%86%D8%B2%D9%87%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%B4%D8%AA%D8%A7%D9%82_Arabe_2221_BNF.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
